menu "app_cycle -- wake and sleep"

config APP_CYCLE_INTERVAL_MIN
    int "Minutes between wakes"
    default 30
    range 5 720
    help
        Wakes land on the wall-clock grid (:00 and :30 by default). Each wake costs a
        Wi-Fi association and a TLS fetch per calendar, a few seconds at ~100 mA; the
        panel refreshes only when the picture changed.

config APP_CYCLE_QUIET_START_H
    int "Quiet hours start (local hour)"
    default 23
    range 0 23

config APP_CYCLE_QUIET_END_H
    int "Quiet hours end (local hour)"
    default 6
    range 0 23
    help
        No wakes between the start and end hour, local time; the first wake after is on
        the end hour. Set start and end equal to wake around the clock.

config APP_CYCLE_AWAKE_WINDOW_S
    int "Seconds to stay awake for setup or after a long KEY press"
    default 900
    range 60 3600

config APP_CYCLE_OTA_EVERY_H
    int "Hours between update checks"
    default 24
    range 1 168

config APP_CYCLE_SLEEP_ON_USB
    bool "Deep sleep even when USB power is present"
    default y
    help
        Off, a board on USB power stays awake: it redraws on the same grid, keeps its
        web page up and stays reachable for flashing. On, it behaves the same on USB as
        on battery, which is what to test before trusting a battery.

endmenu
